IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg2-support`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: sections 146 and 147 -- SUBMISSION OF MATTERS FOR STOCKHOLDER VOTE; AUTHORIZATION
-- OF AGREEMENTS AND OTHER INSTRUMENTS (approval in substantially final form, and ratification before a filing takes effect).
--
-- SEAT: a director whose board approves a merger agreement or an amendment; a stockholder who is promised a vote. Cross-references taken
-- as inputs: sections 204 and 205 (piece dg4), the other ways of ratifying; section 103 (piece dg1), when a filing takes effect.
-- The text is de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a plain-text rendering, not the official text). Both sections' headings carry a bracketed
-- note about the session-law clause that governs their application; that clause is not in the text.

§ `Section 146: a vote of the stockholders the board no longer recommends`

-- "A corporation may agree to submit a matter to a vote of its stockholders whether or not the board of directors determines at any time
-- subsequent to approving such matter that such matter is no longer advisable and recommends that the stockholders reject or vote against
-- the matter." The power does not depend on the board's later view: TRUE either way.
-- src:459 | A corporation may agree to submit a matter to a vote of its stockholders whether or not the board of directors determines at any time subsequent to approving such matter that such matter is no longer advisable and recommends that the stockholders reject or vote against the matter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 146 (src:459)
GIVEN `the board of directors has determined, after approving the matter, that it is no longer advisable and recommends that the stockholders reject it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 146 the corporation may agree to submit the matter to a vote of its stockholders` `the board of directors has determined, after approving the matter, that it is no longer advisable and recommends that the stockholders reject it` MEANS
    TRUE

§ `Section 147: approval in substantially final form, and ratification`

DECLARE `s 147 Form in which the board approves` IS ONE OF
    `in final form`
    `in substantially final form`
    `in some other form`

-- "Whenever this chapter expressly requires the board of directors to approve or take other action with respect to any agreement,
-- instrument or document, such agreement, instrument or document may be approved by the board of directors in final form or in
-- substantially final form." Another form: the text does not say.
-- src:463 | Whenever this chapter expressly requires the board of directors to approve or take other action with respect to any agreement, instrument or document, such agreement, instrument or document may be approved by the board of directors in final form or in substantially final form. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 147 (src:463)
GIVEN `this chapter expressly requires the board of directors to approve or take other action with respect to the agreement, instrument or document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form` IS A `s 147 Form in which the board approves`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147 the board of directors may approve the agreement, instrument or document in this form` `this chapter expressly requires the board of directors to approve or take other action with respect to the agreement, instrument or document` `the form` MEANS
    IF   NOT `this chapter expressly requires the board of directors to approve or take other action with respect to the agreement, instrument or document`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the form`
         WHEN `in final form` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `in substantially final form` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `in some other form` THEN NOTHING

-- "If the board of directors shall have acted to approve or take other action with respect to an agreement, instrument or document that
-- is required by this chapter to be filed with the Secretary of State or referenced in any certificate so filed, the board of directors
-- may, at any time after providing such approval or taking such other action and prior to the effectiveness of such filing with the
-- Secretary of State, adopt a resolution ratifying the agreement, instrument or document." After the filing is effective this section
-- does not give the power (sections 204 and 205 and the common law may).
-- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1): when a filing becomes effective is theirs; whether it has is a plain input.
-- src:463 | If the board of directors shall have acted to approve or take other action with respect to an agreement, instrument or document that is required by this chapter to be filed with the Secretary of State or referenced in any certificate so filed, the board of directors may, at any time after providing such approval or taking such other action and prior to the effectiveness of such filing with the Secretary of State, adopt a resolution ratifying the agreement, instrument or document. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 147 (src:463)
GIVEN `the board of directors has acted to approve or take other action with respect to the agreement, instrument or document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement, instrument or document is required by this chapter to be filed with the Secretary of State or referenced in a certificate so filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the filing with the Secretary of State has not yet become effective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 147 the board of directors may adopt a resolution ratifying the agreement, instrument or document` `the board of directors has acted to approve or take other action with respect to the agreement, instrument or document` `the agreement, instrument or document is required by this chapter to be filed with the Secretary of State or referenced in a certificate so filed` `the filing with the Secretary of State has not yet become effective` MEANS
        `the board of directors has acted to approve or take other action with respect to the agreement, instrument or document`
    AND `the agreement, instrument or document is required by this chapter to be filed with the Secretary of State or referenced in a certificate so filed`
    AND `the filing with the Secretary of State has not yet become effective`

-- "A ratification under this section shall be deemed to be effective as of the time of the original approval or other action by the board
-- of directors". The text speaks of a time; this module carries the date of the original approval.
-- src:463 | A ratification under this section shall be deemed to be effective as of the time of the original approval or other action by the board of directors …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 147 (src:463)
GIVEN `the date of the original approval or other action by the board of directors` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 147 the date as of which the ratification is effective` `the date of the original approval or other action by the board of directors` MEANS
    `the date of the original approval or other action by the board of directors`

-- "...and to satisfy any requirement under this chapter that the board of directors approve or take other action with respect to such
-- agreement, instrument or document in a specific manner or sequence."
-- src:463 | and to satisfy any requirement under this chapter that the board of directors approve or take other action with respect to such agreement, instrument or document in a specific manner or sequence. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 147 (src:463)
GIVEN `the ratification is a ratification under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147 the ratification satisfies a requirement that the board of directors approve or act in a specific manner or sequence` `the ratification is a ratification under this section` MEANS
    IF   `the ratification is a ratification under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "Ratification under this section shall not be deemed to be the exclusive means of ratifying an agreement, instrument or document
-- approved by the board of directors pursuant to this section, but shall be in addition to any ratification or validation that may be
-- available under §§ 204 and 205 of this title or under the common law."
-- out of range: sections 204 and 205 (piece dg4): the other ratification the text mentions; not read here.
-- src:463 | Ratification under this section shall not be deemed to be the exclusive means of ratifying an agreement, instrument or document approved by the board of directors pursuant to this section, but shall be in addition to any ratification or validation that may be available under §§ 204 and 205 of this title or under the common law.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 147 (src:463)
GIVEN `the agreement, instrument or document was approved by the board of directors pursuant to this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 147 ratification under this section is the exclusive means of ratifying it` `the agreement, instrument or document was approved by the board of directors pursuant to this section` MEANS
    FALSE
